"Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Possible Events in the Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future tense (<span class=\"strong\">will</span>) to talk about actions in the future. You can also use the modals <span class=\"strong\">might </span> and <span class=\"strong\">may </span> to talk about possible actions in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will </span> goes before the verb. The short form is<span class=\"strong\"> 'll</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Future tense when you talk about the future, make offers or make predictions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The modals <span class=\"strong\">might </span> and <span class=\"strong\">may </span> go before the verb. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They talk about future possibility or chance that something will happen. <br><span class=\"strong\">Might </span> means there is a smaller chance that something will happen (30%). <br><span class=\"strong\">May </span> means there is a slightly greater chance that something will happen (50%).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "&nbsp;", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Past Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Continuous Tense to talk about an action that was happening in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You often use the Past Continuous tense and the Simple Past tense together in a sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use both of these tenses to talk about an action that interrupted another action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you <span class=\"strong\">rang </span >, (Simple Past) I <span class=\"strong\">was getting</span> ready to leave (Past Continuous).", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cops", "type": "name"}, {"content": "casual word for police ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The cops came and interviewed us.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to show up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to appear ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The cops showed up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "jerk ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a rude person ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He is such a jerk!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "obnoxious", "type": "name"}, {"content": " loud and rude ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He was very obnoxious at the restaurant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to yell", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to talk very loudly at someone ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He was yelling at his ex-girlfriend.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "forgiving ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "soft-hearted; ready to forgive people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: Maybe I'm too forgiving.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "flaw ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an imperfection; a mistake", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: Everyone has character flaws.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to make up", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to be friends again after an argument ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Marco and I made up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le12ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": " Form a group of six people. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The first person thinks of a Past Continuous and Past tense sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The first person whispers (says it VERY quietly) to the second person, who then whispers it to the next person, etc.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The last person says the sentence out loud. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Is it the same as the original sentence? ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Play it 6 times so everyone has a chance to think of a sentence.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I think of sentences in the Past Continuous and Past tenses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I whisper it to the next person.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I say the sentence out loud.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le12ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn5le12ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "", "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn5le12ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<sp